      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 04-340, San Remo Hotel v. the City and County of San Francisco."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Well, what are your -\u00ad exactly what claims are -- is your client now raising in Federal court? I mean, we don't take a case to just decide if something is unfair. What are the precise claims your client is raising now in Federal court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "San Remo Hotel (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. UTRECHT: Our -- our primary position is that issue preclusion does not apply for the same reasons that this Court found that issue preclusion did not apply in England when you were required to do two separate litigations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is -- excuse me. Is -- is it your position that there is an exaction here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But am I right? I'm just trying to narrow the issue in my mind. Am I right you want to raise one, two, three, four, or five of those issues that I just described and nothing more?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I interrupt? Because I'm just not following one part of your argument. Are you saying that the Pennsylvania analysis, the ad hoc analysis, was not made in the State court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "City",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the city-- the city contends that -- that a decision in our favor would result in"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they found that the facts that we alleged did not give rise to a right to compensation under State law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Their complaints allege a Penn Central violation, but their briefs in the lower court -- in the lower Federal courts in this proceeding and in the State courts don't discuss Penn Central at all, as the California Supreme Court in footnote 14 of its opinion explained."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Conference of State Chief Justices",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Conference of State Chief Justices have filed an amicus brief in support actually of us in this case, saying we don't see that the facts of this case present the question on which you granted review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let's take a -- may I -- may I, in effect, approach it with a simpler example, which -\u00ad which is not this case, but I -- I just want to know how -- how the -- the systems work together."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-04-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58da22971ee779f15e8ff9780efe2356ff1f5068991d4825bc11762e98c0fea0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58da22971ee7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, in this case they went first to the Superior Court in San Francisco and they filed an administrative mandamus claim challenging the zoning determination that was made in their case because they're in a historic district."
    }
  ],
